%% GDPR Delete Pipeline — End-to-End
flowchart TD
    User[User submits<br/>Delete Request] --> Intake[Intake Service<br/>+ Identity Verification]
    Intake --> Reg[Delete Request Log<br/>(append-only, signed)]
    Intake --> Discovery[Discovery Service]

    Discovery --> Cat[Data Catalog<br/>(Hive / Glue / Unity)]
    Discovery --> Lineage[Lineage Graph<br/>(DataHub / OpenLineage)]
    Discovery --> Locations[User Data Locations<br/>(tables, keys, indices)]

    Locations --> Coord[Delete Coordinator<br/>(Temporal workflow)]

    Coord --> Ice[Iceberg Adapter<br/>DELETE WHERE user_id = X]
    Coord --> WH[Warehouse Adapter<br/>DELETE FROM ...]
    Coord --> Cache[Redis Adapter<br/>DEL user:X]
    Coord --> S3[S3 Adapter<br/>lifecycle + version purge]
    Coord --> ES[Elasticsearch Adapter<br/>delete_by_query]
    Coord --> FS[Feature Store Adapter<br/>mark deleted]
    Coord --> ML[ML Dataset Adapter<br/>exclude / regenerate]
    Coord --> Crypto[Crypto-Shredding<br/>kms:ScheduleKeyDeletion]

    Ice --> Receipt[Receipt Aggregator<br/>(signed, immutable)]
    WH --> Receipt
    Cache --> Receipt
    S3 --> Receipt
    ES --> Receipt
    FS --> Receipt
    ML --> Receipt
    Crypto --> Receipt

    Receipt --> Verify[Verification Service<br/>(re-discover = 0)]
    Verify --> Report[Compliance Report<br/>(PDF + crypto receipt)]
    Report --> Audit[Audit Ledger<br/>(7+ yr retention)]
    Report --> Notify[Notify User]
